<title>INDONESIA: Two missing after Indonesian ship sinks.</title>
<headline>Two missing after Indonesian ship sinks.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian rescue officials said on Monday two crew members were missing after an Indonesian coastal vessel sank in rough seas off East Java.</p>
<p>The officials said 12 of the 14 crew had been rescued after the MV Wahana Utama V sank on Saturday. The search for the missing two was continuing.</p>
<p>The vessel, carrying 800 tonnes of cement, went down off the north coast of Madura Island, the officials said.</p>
<p>No further details were available.</p>
</text>
